'''Beggars''' are a group of randomly occurring [[NPC]]s in the game. There are a total of 8 types of beggars, each requesting different donations. Isaac can donate pennies, keys, hearts, or {{dlc|a}} bombs by simply walking into them. With each donation, the beggar has a chance to drop various [[pickup]]s and [[trinket]]s. Sometimes, the beggar will drop an [[item]] and disappear. The rate of drops isn't influenced by [[luck]].

Beggars can be destroyed by {{e|Bomb||bombs}}, causing them to drop a few pickups. {{dlc|nr}} If destroyed in {{s|Chest}} or {{s|Dark Room}} they will drop an item, with the exception of the Shell Game who still drops pickups.

Normal Beggars, Devil Beggars, or more rarely Key Masters, Bomb Bums, Battery Bums, and Rotten Beggars can be spawned using {{p|XX - Judgement}}.

== Beggar ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Beggar
 | id      = 6
 | variant = 4
}}

'''Beggars''' ask for {{e|Penny|text=Pennies}}. For each payout, they have a chance to drop the following
* 16.6% {{e|Red Heart|text=Heart}} (3.33% with {{t|Daemon's Tail}})
* 16.6% {{e|Bomb}} (23.3% with {{t|Daemon's Tail}})
* 16.6% {{e|Key}} (23.3% with {{t|Daemon's Tail}})
* 25% [[Cards and Runes|Card]]
* 12.6% {{i|Breakfast}}, {{i|Lunch}}, {{i|Dinner}}, {{i|Dessert}}, or {{i|Rotten Meat}}
* 12.6% An item from the {{ip|Beggar|text=Beggar item pool}}
After spawning a pedestal item, the Beggar will disappear and can no longer be donated to.

The hard-coded items can be spawned even if previously encountered during the same run.

=== Notes ===
* When destroyed drops random pickups and increases the {{r|Angel Room}} / {{r|Devil Room}} chance by 35%.
* When paying out increase the {{r|Angel Room}} chance by 10%.
* {{Dlc|r}} The chance for paying out depends on whether the game is in hard mode or not.
** On hard mode, the first time the Beggar pays out will always be after at least six donations, with a high chance of paying out at six. After the first payout, any subsequent payout will take at least three donations.
** On other modes (Normal, Greed, and Greedier), Beggars may pay out after any amount has been donated. It is unclear whether there is a limit, but it is very rare that they take six or more donations before paying out.
** If the player has {{I|Lucky Foot}}, payouts are much more likely on each donation after the first payout. On Hard mode, the minimum amount of donations between each payout after the first is reduced to 2.
{{clear}}

== Devil Beggar ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Devil Beggar
 | variant = 5
}}

'''Devil Beggars''' ask for {{e|Red Heart||hearts}}. Each donation deals a half heart of damage to Isaac (a full heart in [[Chapter 4]] and beyond). For each payout, they have a chance to drop the following
* 25% [[Pill]]
* 25% [[Card]]
* 12.5% [[Trinket]]
* 37.5% An item from the {{ip|Devil Beggar|text=Devil Beggar item pool}}
After spawning a pedestal item, the Devil Beggar will disappear and can no longer be donated to.

=== Notes ===
* {{dlc|nr}} When destroyed drops various [[pickups]] {{dlc|nr+}} and increases the {{r|Angel Room}} chance by 25%.
** {{dlc|r}} When destroyed drops two {{e|Spider||Spiders}}.
** {{dlc|r+}} Increases the {{r|Angel Room}} / {{r|Devil Room}} chance by 35%.
* When paying out decreases the {{r|Angel Room}} chance by 10%.
* {{dlc|nr}} Similar to a {{m|Blood Donation Machine}}, Devil Beggars will take Eternal Hearts first, then Red Hearts. If Isaac only has half a Red Heart remaining, they will then take Black Hearts and Soul Hearts. It is possible to die in this manner.
** {{dlc|r}} Devil Beggars ignore eternal hearts when taking hearts unless Isaac only has half a heart and an eternal heart; at that point, the beggar will take the eternal heart instead of the half heart.
** {{Dlc|r}} The Devil Beggar will take the last Half Red Heart before Black Hearts and Soul Hearts.
* [[Invulnerability]] and [[shield]]s can be used to prevent damage from it.
* The full hearts of damage in [[Chapter 4]] and beyond can be mitigated by {{i|The Wafer}}, {{i|Cancer}}, or [[Percs]], which cut it back down to 1/2 heart.
* The donations activate damage effects, such as {{i|Celtic Cross}}.
* Activating Devil Beggars while using an item that grants invincibility, such as the {{i|Book of Shadows}} or {{p|Algiz}}, will not lower Isaac's health, but will still cause the beggar to spawn items. {{i|Holy Mantle}} is ignored, though, so {{c|The Lost}} will be killed instantly.
** {{dlc|nr}} It is possible to exploit the invincibility frames after taking damage to donate twice for the price of one donation. {{t|Blind Rage}} doubles the invincibility frames, thus allowing to activate the Devil Beggar even more times in that period.
** {{e|Bone Heart||Bone Hearts}} will not be broken by donating to a Devil Beggar unless Isaac has no other hearts, and can drain multiple Bone Hearts without breaking them.
* {{Dlc|r}} The chance for paying out depends on whether the game is in hard mode or not.
** On [[Hard mode]], the first time the Devil Beggar pays out will always be after at least 6 donations, though it very rarely takes more than 6. After the first payout, any subsequent payout will take at least three donations.
** On other modes (Normal, Greed, and Greedier), Devil Beggars will pay out randomly between donations 1-7, with increasing odds and a guaranteed payout after 8 donations. The chances of getting subsequent payouts are slightly higher than the chances of getting the first.
** If the player has {{I|Lucky Foot}}, payouts are much more likely on each donation after the first payout. On Hard mode, the minimum amount of donations between each payout after the first is reduced to 2.
{{clear}}

== Key Master ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Key Master
 | variant = 7
}}

'''Key Masters''' (also known as Key Bums) are rare and ask for {{e|Key||keys}}. For each donation they drop the following
* 65% Nothing
* 30.6% Random [[Chest]]
* 4.4% {{t|Paper Clip}} or An item from the {{ip|Key Master|text=Key Master item pool}} if the Paper Clip has been encountered in the run
After spawning a pedestal item or dropping {{t|Paper Clip}}, the Key Master will disappear and can no longer be donated to.

=== Notes ===
* When destroyed drops random pickups {{dlc|r+}} and increases the {{r|Angel Room}} / {{r|Devil Room}} chance by 35%.
* {{dlc|r+}} When paying out increase the {{r|Angel Room}} chance by 10%.
* If found on {{s|Dark Room}} or {{s|Chest}}, the chest payouts will contain items.
* {{dlc|nr+}} Possessing a {{e|Golden Key}} will not affect the Key Master in any way.
** {{dlc|r+}} Possessing a {{e|Golden Key}} will now make the Key Master instantly pay out with an item, consuming the Golden Key as well.
