== Bomb Bum ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = a
 | name    = Bomb Bum
 | variant = 9
}}

'''Bomb Bums''' ask for {{e|Bomb||bombs}}.

{{dlc|nr}} For every donation, they have a chance to drop 1-2 Bombs or an item from the {{ip|Bomb Bum|text=Bomb Bum item pool}}. After spawning a pedestal item, the Bomb Bum will disappear.

{{dlc|r}} For each donation they drop the following
* 60% Nothing
* 26% 1-3 {{e|Penny}}
* 9% {{e|Red Heart||Heart}} 
* 5% An item from the {{ip|Bomb Bum|text=Bomb Bum item pool}}
After spawning a pedestal item the Bomb Bum will disappear and can no longer be donated to.

=== Notes ===
* When destroyed drops various [[pickups]] and {{dlc|r+}} increases the {{r|Angel Room}} / {{r|Devil Room}} chance by 35%.
* {{dlc|r+}} When paying out increase the {{r|Angel Room}} chance by 10%.
* {{dlc|nr}} Bomb Bums are rarer than other beggars.
* {{dlc|nr}} It is possible that the Bomb Bum will "pay out" by spawning a Troll Bomb underneath itself.
* {{dlc|nr+}} Possessing a {{e|Golden Bomb}} will not affect the Bomb Bum in any way.
** {{dlc|r+}} Possessing a {{e|Golden Bomb}} will now make the Bomb Bum instantly pay out with an item, consuming the Golden Bomb as well.
* {{dlc+|r}} Bomb Bums are immune to bombs, and will respond to an attempt to bombing them by spawning several troll bombs, similar to {{p|XVI - The Tower}}.
** Bomb Bums can still be destroyed by the shockwave from {{i|Mama Mega!}} and {{i|Larynx}}, by being walked into with the effect of {{i|Mega Mush}}, or by the explosion of {{i|Dr. Fetus}} and {{i|Epic Fetus}} with {{i|Terra}}.
** Having {{t|Safety Scissors}} allows Isaac to acquire infinite bombs by bombing the beggar repeatedly.
*** Can be abused further for infinite pickups with {{i|Sack Head}}.{{dlc-}}
