== Shell Game ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Shell Game
 | variant = 6
}}

'''Shell Game''' beggars can sometimes be found in the {{r|Arcade}}; they also have a small chance to spawn elsewhere. After giving the beggar a coin, they will lift a skull, revealing a Penny, Bomb, Red Heart, Key, or {{i|Skatole}}. The beggar will shuffle the skulls around and wait for Isaac to bump into 1 of the 3 shells. 

If Isaac wins then they will payout with 2 of the respective pickup / {{i|Skatole}}. If Isaac loses they'll instead spawn an {{e|Attack Fly}}. 

Skatole has a 7.6% of being chosen while the other pickups have a 23.1% of being chosen. 

{{Dlc|r}} If Isaac wins a coin pickup, the beggar will spawn 2-3 coins.

Once {{i|Skatole}} is dropped the Shell Game will disappear.
=== Notes ===
* {{i|Lucky Foot}} increases chances of winning from 33% to 55%.
* If {{i|Skatole}} has already been acquired, other Shell Games will never give a second {{i|Skatole}} and will remain unless destroyed.
** If Isaac wishes to avoid a {{i|Skatole}} pickup (for example, he wants to acquire more pickups), he may leave the room — this resets the Shell Game (though his spent coin is lost).
* Item payouts are subjected to the same spawning chances as usual. {{e|Bomb||Bombs}} can be replaced with {{e|Troll Bomb||Troll Bombs}} or {{e|Double Bomb||Double Bombs}}, {{e|Red Heart||Red Hearts}} can be replaced with {{e|Half Red Heart||Half Red Hearts}}, {{e|Soul Heart||Soul Hearts}}, {{e|Black Heart||Black Hearts}}, {{e|Eternal Heart||Eternal Hearts}}, or {{e|Bone Heart||Bone Hearts}}, and {{e|Penny||Pennies}} can be replaced with {{e|Nickel||Nickels}} or {{e|Dime||Dimes}}.
** Under the effects of {{i|Humbleing Bundle}}, bombs will be Double Bombs, Red Hearts will be Double Hearts, and Keys will be Key Rings.
* {{dlc+|r}} A {{ip|Shell Game|text="shellGame" item pool}} contains other items than just {{i|Skatole}}. However, the item pool is currently only used by the {{i|Bag of Crafting}}, which commonly draws from it when the {{c|Tainted ???}} exclusive {{e|Poop Nugget}} is included in the recipe.{{dlc-}}
{{clear}}

== Hell Game ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Hell Game
 | variant     = 15
 | unlocked by = Hell Game
}}

'''Hell Game''' beggars can sometimes be found in the {{r|Arcade}}; they also have a small chance to spawn elsewhere. After giving the beggar health, they will lift a skull, revealing a Black Heart, Blue Spider, Bomb, Key, Coin, Card, or an item from the {{ip|Devil Room|text=Devil item pool}}. The beggar will shuffle the skulls around and wait for Isaac to bump into 1 of the 3 shells. 

If Isaac wins then they will payout with a Black Heart, 2 Blue Spiders, 2 Bombs, 2 Keys, 2-3 Coins, A Card/Rune (Will always show a tarot card), or the shown item respectively. If Isaac loses they'll instead spawn a {{e|Spider}}. 

The {{ip|Devil Room|text=Devil Room Item}} has a 7.6% of being chosen while the other pickups have a 15.4% of being chosen. 

=== Notes ===
* {{i|Lucky Foot}} increases chances of winning from 33% to 55%.
* [[Invulnerability]] and [[shield]]s can be used to prevent damage from it.
* Like with the Shell Game, pickups spawn under the same rules and chances as usual.
* The item shown in each Hell Game will not change between plays. This means that Isaac can't just leave the room and try to get a different item. Isaac can, however, leave the room if he wishes to prevent the Hell Game from disappearing (though the spent health will be lost).
* Unlike the devil beggar, bombing a Hell Game beggar does not affect the chance for an angel room to appear. Like the devil beggar, however, it will spawn spiders.
* {{T|Sigil of Baphomet|nr+}}: the invincibility after killing an enemy can be used to play for free. Since the Hell Game spawns a spider when Isaac loses, this can be used to get a free play after every loss.

Will be replaced with a {{m|Devil Beggar}} if not unlocked.
{{clear}}{{dlc clear}}

